1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,880
I'm John Strohmeyer and I'm a Troop Order of the Arrow

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:06,800
Representative Advisor with Troop 55 in Houston, Texas.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,080
This edition of the Scoutmaster podcast

4
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:10,880
is sponsored by backers like me,

5
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:13,320
And now it's the old Scoutmaster.

6
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:19,360
["Scoutmaster"]

7
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:24,360
One of my favorite authors is. this quote is attributed to him,

8
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:26,480
And I'm talking about Mark Twain.

9
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,960
He probably didn't actually say it.

10
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:31,760
If you're a Mark Twain fan, it really does sound like him.

11
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:33,360
But here is what he said,

12
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:36,880
And I think this is a great thing for fathers everywhere

13
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:38,040
to know.

14
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,760
He said: when I was a boy of 14, my father was so ignorant

15
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:47,080
I could hardly stand to have the old man around.

16
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:50,480
But when I got to be 21,, I was astonished

17
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:54,360
at how much the old man had learned in seven years.

18
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:57,400
["Scoutmaster"].

19
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:00,480
It's called the Twain effect.

20
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:05,840
So if you're the father, or the mother, indeed- of a 14-year-old-

21
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:10,120
and yeah, they don't

22
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:10,920
Just wait,

23
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:11,480
Just wait,

24
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:12,080
It'll happen-

25
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:13,720
The Twain effect works.

26
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:17,080
Hey, this is podcast number 316..

27
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:17,580
Hey,

28
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:20,580
["Scoutmaster"].

29
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:44,580
Welcome back to the Scoutmaster podcast.

30
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:46,060
This is Clark Green.

31
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:47,660
Let's see, looking in the mailbag.

32
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:50,540
Actually, this came from one of the chats that we have,

33
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:54,740
And every Tuesday and Wednesday morning,

34
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:57,180
just about every Tuesday and Wednesday morning,

35
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:59,500
I'll be at scoutmastercgcom

36
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,180
And we'll have a live chat

37
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:02,620
And a lot of people show up and we

38
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:06,340
discuss all kinds of things, sometimes really important things,

39
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:08,220
And sometimes we just talk about the weather,

40
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:10,780
where we went camping or something like that.

41
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:14,340
So look at the Facebook feed and the Twitter feed

42
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:18,700
And watch for an announcement that the live chat is happening

43
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:20,260
on Tuesday and Wednesday mornings.

44
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:21,460
Come along and join us.

45
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:23,140
But on the live chat this past week

46
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:27,140
I heard from a parent and a committee member and a mom.

47
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:30,300
She signed on and she said: our scoutmaster

48
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:33,980
has heard that he can hold up rank advancement at a Scoutmaster

49
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:37,340
conference for not showing scout spirit.

50
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:39,060
I understand the concept, I think,

51
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:42,580
but I wonder how this should be done and communicated

52
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:45,620
to a scout that's excited about moving up in rank

53
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:48,540
and who has met all the requirements.

54
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:50,540
And my reply was: you know,

55
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:52,340
that's really not quite how it works.

56
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:55,620
A scoutmaster conference is just that: a conference.

57
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:58,980
A scout does not pass or fail a conference.

58
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:02,420
They just sit down with the scoutmaster and they have a talk.

59
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:06,580
And as for the requirement to demonstrate scout spirit

60
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:09,620
by living the scout oath and law,

61
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:12,180
well, that's not really a pass or fail

62
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:15,060
kind of a requirement, is it?

63
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:17,300
I never considered it to be one,

64
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:19,780
And it's not something that a scoutmaster evaluates

65
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:23,700
using their own judgment. because what is the requirement?

66
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:26,420
Demonstrate scout spirit by living the scout oath

67
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:29,340
and law. and the scout in the earlier rank

68
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:32,540
shares four points of the scout law.

69
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:37,540
It gives examples how they have been living the ideals

70
00:03:37,540 --> 00:03:39,420
in those four points. right,

71
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:41,340
I don't see that as being a pass fail thing.

72
00:03:41,460 --> 00:03:44,420
I think it's a wonderful conversation to have with a scout

73
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:47,420
and maybe- yeah, maybe- you encourage them to do more

74
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:51,500
or you congratulate them on doing just a marvelous job with it,

75
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:56,500
But I can't see failing that requirement.

76
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:58,500
I don't know how you would do that.

77
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:03,060
Then they replied: well, if a scoutmaster has a scout

78
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:06,300
he thinks is moving too fast through the ranks

79
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,740
or is having behavior issues

80
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:13,780
or whom the scoutmaster considers to be immature,

81
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:17,100
he should not be using the scout spirit excuse

82
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:18,540
to slow them down. then-

83
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:21,780
And my reply was yes, that's absolutely the point.

84
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:25,500
So the resource that you wanna look at to explain this

85
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:28,020
is the Guide to Advancement,

86
00:04:28,020 --> 00:04:30,140
where it talks about scoutmaster conferences,

87
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:34,500
and I will have a link to that resource

88
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:36,460
in the podcast notes for you.

89
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:38,380
And I wanna challenge a couple of other things

90
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:39,740
that you said here.

91
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:42,420
It's impossible for a scout to move too fast

92
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:43,700
through the requirements.

93
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:47,340
There's no reference to age or maturity

94
00:04:47,340 --> 00:04:49,380
in any of the rank requirements.

95
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:51,300
The only time we see age mentioned

96
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:54,060
is when a boy joins a scout troop.

97
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:56,540
So that's already all been taken care of

98
00:04:56,540 --> 00:05:01,219
And I would probably suggest that you don't try

99
00:05:01,219 --> 00:05:03,219
to argue with the scoutmaster

100
00:05:03,219 --> 00:05:05,800
because they don't understand what they're doing.

101
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,920
I would think about very seriously

102
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,480
just finding another troop

103
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,400
where the scoutmaster understands scouting,

104
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:13,880
because the one that you're working with doesn't.

105
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:15,680
Now the conversation went on from there

106
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:18,720
and there were other things that kind of pointed out

107
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:21,080
that this particular scoutmaster

108
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:24,000
really had very little idea of what their job was.

109
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:28,760
The people in the position to make any kind of change

110
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:29,640
within a scout troop,

111
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:30,600
that's the committee chair

112
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,960
and the charter organization representative.

113
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:35,000
If they're not going to tell the scoutmaster,

114
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,800
who does not understand their work,

115
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:39,080
what changes they need to make,

116
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:41,360
then I think it's just time to find a new troop.

117
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:43,180
It's not that big a deal.

118
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:45,880
It seems like a very big deal until you're done

119
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:47,440
and you found a new troop,

120
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:49,520
because I hear from people who've done that

121
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:50,800
and it works out.

122
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:54,280
There's no reason to subject your children.

123
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,960
I understand that something like that's gonna be

124
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:56,800
a little upsetting.

125
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:57,960
it's gonna be a bit of a challenge,

126
00:05:57,960 --> 00:06:02,120
but I hear from people who go ahead and change troops

127
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:05,000
and then they find out that that was a very good idea.

128
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,640
I've had lots of scouts over the years

129
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:10,680
who have come to our troop from a different troop

130
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:13,120
because it just wasn't working for them,

131
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:14,960
and I've had some of my scouts

132
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:16,740
our troop doesn't quite work for them

133
00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:18,160
and they go to another troop.

134
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,400
That's fine,

135
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:21,160
I have no problem with that.

