208
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:06,200
Scouts Mastership in Seven Minutes or Less.

209
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:36,560
So the big idea here is that scouting

210
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:41,360
is something for scouts to discover.

211
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:46,480
One of the perennial things that we discuss is leadership.

212
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:48,680
Leadership is one of those magic scouting words

213
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:49,720
we think we understand,

214
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:53,200
but few of us really appreciate the length and breadth

215
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:55,600
of just what that magic word implies

216
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,560
when we start applying it to scouting.

217
00:09:57,560 --> 00:10:00,720
So today I wanna talk about leadership

218
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:04,640
as something that scouts get to discover for themselves.

219
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:06,280
I wanna see if I can get you to come along

220
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:09,480
and really think about this, really examine this idea.

221
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:12,040
Now, one of the things I frequently hear from scouters

222
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,920
is that our youth leaders just don't do

223
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:15,000
what they're supposed to do.

224
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,960
They don't seem to have any initiative,

225
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:20,040
And what I hear when somebody says that,

226
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:23,080
what they're telling me is that their scouts

227
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:27,640
don't seem to care about the expectations

228
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:29,360
that adults have set for them.

229
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:31,800
So what these scouters have usually done

230
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:34,840
is they have set themselves up as the leader,

231
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:38,800
as the ones who approve or disapprove of what scouts do.

232
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:41,040
In other words, they have reserved

233
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:44,200
all of the actual authority and power to themselves.

234
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,640
They're waiting for the scouts

235
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:47,760
in some way to prove themselves

236
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:49,480
And after one or two tries

237
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:54,440
and the scouts don't respond as the adults want them to,

238
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:56,280
they usually don't try it again.

239
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:59,080
They oh no, we tried that a couple of times

240
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,560
and it really didn't work.

241
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:02,680
They don't like the way the scouts responded,

242
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:04,760
So they stop trying that

243
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,840
and they end up just taking over

244
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:08,520
and doing everything for the scouts.

245
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,960
I mean, a lot of us have the idea

246
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:12,360
that adults in scouting hold all the cards

247
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:15,000
and deal them out to the scouts as they see fit.

248
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,120
but that's really not scouting at all

249
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,560
And you aren't getting the whole idea of leadership

250
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:21,280
if you see yourself that way,

251
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:23,400
And where this gets complicated is: yes,

252
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:25,600
you are the adult in the equation

253
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:28,000
and you do have all the authority,

254
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,520
because you're there to referee

255
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:31,800
and make sure the things don't go wrong,

256
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:33,720
And naturally, we wouldn't just sit back

257
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:36,840
and watch young people do untoward or dangerous things-

258
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:39,800
They are, after all, in our care-

259
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:42,960
But, in another sense, you are not the authority.

260
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:45,400
You are not the person who must be placated

261
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:49,480
or pleased or served by what your scouts do.

262
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:53,080
That's not the kind of leadership your scouts want or need.

263
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:55,560
You aren't the personification of excellence

264
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,040
and the keeper of standards.

265
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:59,160
All of that work has already been done for you.

