begins to break down. but did you get it?

533
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:54,680
Does the analogy work for you?

534
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:56,840
Of course the pyramid is scouting:

535
00:21:56,879 --> 00:21:59,760
A discovery that you share with young people,

536
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:01,959
not by explaining it to them,

537
00:22:01,959 --> 00:22:06,439
but through their own sense of inquisitiveness and discovery.

538
00:22:06,439 --> 00:22:08,760
Now let's loop back to where we began.

539
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:11,040
We began with the idea of leadership.

540
00:22:11,040 --> 00:22:13,760
Scouting belongs to scouts

541
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:18,159
who lead themselves through the scouting experience right.

542
00:22:18,159 --> 00:22:20,480
It does not belong to adults.

543
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:23,679
Scouters are not the chief executive officers.

544
00:22:23,679 --> 00:22:26,080
They are mentors and enablers.

545
00:22:26,120 --> 00:22:29,199
Scouting is not a useful set of skills we need to teach

546
00:22:29,199 --> 00:22:31,840
or object lessons we have to explain.

547
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:35,919
It is a unique path of discovery with opportunities

548
00:22:35,919 --> 00:22:39,439
to learn those skills and those object lessons

549
00:22:39,439 --> 00:22:41,199
and experience growth.

550
00:22:41,199 --> 00:22:46,199
Scouting is not a program we prepare and present to scouts.

551
00:22:46,439 --> 00:22:50,520
It is a program based on the magic of discovery

552
00:22:50,520 --> 00:22:54,040
and things that they learn for themselves

553
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:56,000
and then they're able to turn around

554
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,120
and share with others.

555
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:59,680
So for our scouts- and I'm speaking of our scouts

556
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:04,680
of every age, from joeys and beavers to cubs,

557
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:07,320
and ventures and rovers-

558
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:10,920
it's about discovering scouting for yourself,

559
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:14,880
under your own steam, under your own leadership,

560
00:23:14,880 --> 00:23:19,000
exercised in correspondence with your age and your abilities.

561
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,880
And rather than explaining exactly how that works

562
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:23,920
across all ages and abilities,

563
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:26,880
let me refer you to a post I wrote earlier this year

564
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:28,880
called Every Scout is a Leader,

565
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:31,920
And I'll have a link to that post in the podcast notes.

566
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:35,120
In that post I lay out four types of leadership

567
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:37,200
Basically. first, you lead yourself.

568
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:39,680
Second, you follow cooperatively.

569
00:23:39,680 --> 00:23:42,040
Third, you help your fellow scouts.

570
00:23:42,040 --> 00:23:43,960
And fourth, you shape the directions

571
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:45,920
and plans of your patrol and troop.

572
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:47,880
Now you really can't skip any of those steps,

573
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:50,640
so you have to start where your scouts are.

574
00:23:50,640 --> 00:23:52,440
And I'm not going to say

575
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:55,160
that adults aren't leaders in scouting,

576
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:57,120
because we definitely are.

577
00:23:57,120 --> 00:24:00,160
It's just the kind of leaders that we need to be.

578
00:24:00,160 --> 00:24:02,680
We need to be responsive leaders.

579
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:05,840
Our response and our level of involvement

580
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:08,740
in what is happening needs to correspond

581
00:24:08,740 --> 00:24:11,320
with the growing abilities of our scouts.

582
00:24:11,320 --> 00:24:13,520
You can't just decide.

583
00:24:13,520 --> 00:24:16,080
if you're in a scout troop, for example,

584
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:18,600
you can't just decide, okay,

585
00:24:18,600 --> 00:24:20,480
we're going to be youth led now,

586
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:22,660
and throw a switch and walk away.

587
00:24:22,660 --> 00:24:24,400
It's not instantaneous.

588
00:24:24,400 --> 00:24:27,360
Youth leadership is not throwing a switch.

589
00:24:27,360 --> 00:24:30,160
It's more like planting a seed. okay,

590
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:33,760
And I know more analogies, right,

591
00:24:33,760 --> 00:24:35,360
Okay, just bear with me.

592
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:37,480
If we throw a light switch and the light

593
00:24:37,480 --> 00:24:40,360
doesn't come on right away, we get impatient.

594
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:42,800
But if we plant a seed and it doesn't sprout

595
00:24:42,800 --> 00:24:45,480
in 10 seconds, well, we aren't surprised.

596
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:48,660
We know that this sort of thing takes time.

597
00:24:48,660 --> 00:24:50,900
You can't plant a seed and go boop

598
00:24:50,900 --> 00:24:53,340
and the next minute have an oak tree right.

599
00:24:53,340 --> 00:24:54,540
It takes some time.

600
00:24:54,540 --> 00:24:57,300
So what's in that seed that causes it to grow?

601
00:24:57,300 --> 00:24:59,820
There's tremendous potential in there,

602
00:24:59,820 --> 00:25:01,620
but it has to have the right environment

603
00:25:01,620 --> 00:25:04,860
And the right environment. in scouting,

604
00:25:04,860 --> 00:25:07,980
the mysterious process at the heart of it all

605
00:25:07,980 --> 00:25:09,380
is discovery.

606
00:25:09,380 --> 00:25:12,500
So back to the big analogy. it's back to the pyramid.

607
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:15,960
You're leading because you're getting them there right.

608
00:25:15,960 --> 00:25:18,960
You're getting them to the opportunities.

609
00:25:18,960 --> 00:25:21,680
You don't really create the opportunities quite so much

610
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:24,360
as scouting itself creates the opportunities.

611
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:26,280
And you're keeping an eye on things

612
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:29,080
because, yes, the scouts are in our care,

613
00:25:29,080 --> 00:25:31,960
So we have to have that authority to keep an eye on things,

614
00:25:31,960 --> 00:25:35,800
make sure they're not doing untoward or dangerous things,

615
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:38,560
but we bring them to this place

616
00:25:38,560 --> 00:25:40,800
of opportunity and discovery,

617
00:25:40,800 --> 00:25:42,800
And that's what scouting really is.

